  "question": {
    "text": "A force $\\mathrm{f}=\\mathrm{x}^2 \\mathrm{y} \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+\\mathrm{y}^2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}$ acts on a particle in a plane $\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y}=10$. The work done by this force during a displacement from $(0,0)$ to $(4 \\mathrm{~m}, 2 \\mathrm{~m})$ is $\\qquad$ Joule (round off to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "152",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & y=10-x \\\\ & w=\\int_0^4 x^2(10-x) d x+\\int_0^2 y^2 d y \\\\ & =\\frac{10 x^3}{3}-\\left.\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right|_0 ^4+\\left.\\frac{y^3}{3}\\right|_0 ^2 \\\\ & =\\frac{640}{3}-\\frac{256}{4}+\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ & =216 \\times 64 \\\\ & =152 \\mathrm{~J}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
